# JARVIS — Project Rules

You work on JARVIS, the internal search engine for resolved Jira SLGMS tickets (LAFISE). Follow these conventions in every change.

## Project overview

- Stack: Node.js 18+, CommonJS, Express, EJS, DaisyUI + Tailwind (CDN), gray-matter, csv-parse. No build step, no client framework, no test framework.
- Entry point: `server.js` (`node server.js`, default port `8000`). All data is served from an in-memory note cache — no database.
- Layout: pure logic modules in `lib/`, CLI scripts in `scripts/`, single-page UI in `templates/index.ejs`, user docs in `docs/`, packaging in `release/`.

## Module map (lib/)

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `search-relevance.js` | Result ranking (relevance score, recency sort) |
| `similar-notes.js` | Tokenize / Jaccard similarity; its exported helpers (`tokenize`, `noteFingerprint`, `overlapScore`, `facetMatch`, `combineTokenMaps`) are reused by the insights engine |
| `search-facets.js` | Facet filters, pagination |
| `quality-metrics.js` | Documentation-quality aggregations (by sistema / analista) + global CSAT |
| `insights-engine.js` | Deterministic clustering of recurring incidents (bucket by sistema + strong token → greedy similarity → merge pass) |
| `insights-proposals.js` | Explainable improvement rules per cluster + Markdown export |
| `note-quality.js` | Shared "weak closure" heuristic (`caso atendido` etc.) — do NOT fork this logic |
| `jira-sync.js` / `jira-api.js` / `jira-sync-scheduler.js` | Jira Cloud sync (incremental, API wins over CSV) |
| `jira-satisfaction.js` / `satisfaction-fields.js` | CSAT JSM sync; field helpers split out to break a circular dependency |
| `env.js` | `loadEnv()` — must run before any config-dependent require |

## Code conventions

- CommonJS only: `require` / `module.exports`. Identifiers and code comments in English; UI strings and user docs in neutral Spanish.
- `parseNote` in `server.js` is the single source of note parsing. Scripts reuse it via `require("../server")` — this is why `app.listen` is guarded with `if (require.main === module)`. Keep that guard.
- Notes cache: `NOTES_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 15s). Insights cache: 5 min, keyed by filter params. Any sync/import/reload path must go through `invalidateNotesCache()` — it clears both caches.
- Empty/placeholder fields are normalized to `"N/D"` — treat it as empty, never as a searchable token.
- Sorting by recency uses `jira_updated_at` (with time), not frontmatter `updated`.
- Insights computation is always on-demand behind its cache; never compute it inside `/api/search` or any per-request search path.
- Circular dependency rule: pure field helpers without Jira config live in `satisfaction-fields.js`; anything needing `getConfig()` from `jira-api.js` must lazy-require inside the function, never at module top level.

## UI conventions (templates/index.ejs)

- One vanilla `<script>` block at the end of the template; no frameworks, no modules.
- Always run note-derived data through the existing `escapeHtml()` helper before injecting HTML.
- Modals follow the `quality-modal` pattern: `<dialog class="modal">` + `.modal-box` + `<form method="dialog" class="modal-backdrop">`.
- Navbar buttons: `btn btn-sm btn-ghost text-white border border-white/30` (the navbar has a dark background in both themes).
- Brand accents only via `text-lafise`, `btn-lafise`, `border-lafise/30`.
- Every component must look right in BOTH `lafise-light` and `lafise-dark`: use DaisyUI tokens (`bg-base-200`, `bg-base-100`, `text-base-content`, `border-base-300`) and never hardcode hex colors for surfaces/text.
- Copy-to-clipboard via the existing `copyText(text, toastMessage)` helper (shows the shared toast).
- Theme switching is already implemented (button `#btn-theme-toggle`, `localStorage` key `jarvis-theme`) — don't add another theme mechanism.

## Jira sync & configuration

- API sync always takes priority over CSV import. CSV is a manual backup path only.
- `.env` is gitignored — never commit it, never print tokens in logs or notes.
- Document every new env var in `.env.example` AND in the guides (`docs/guia-instalacion-equipo.*`).
- Sync state lives in `.jarvis/` (gitignored). Notes live in `notes/` (gitignored, distributed via release ZIP).
- Key env vars: `JIRA_BASE_URL`, `JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN`, `JIRA_PROJECT=SLGMS`, `JIRA_SYNC_ON_START`, `JIRA_SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES`, `JIRA_SYNC_SISTEMA_FILTER`, `JIRA_SATISFACTION_SYNC`, `PORT`, `DENDRON_NOTES_DIR`.

## Release & docs

- Version bump touches ALL of: `package.json` version, `LEEME-INSTALACION.txt` header, `docs/guia-analistas-jarvis.md` / `.html`, `docs/guia-instalacion-equipo.md` / `.html` (header + zip filename + novedades table).
- Add an entry at the top of `release/CHANGELOG.md`.
- Build the package with `npm run package:release` (ZIP in `release/`).
- NEVER run `git commit` / `git push` without explicit user authorization.

## Operation & safety

- Port 8000 may be the user's running instance: NEVER kill a process you didn't start. For manual API testing, start a separate instance with a different port (`$env:PORT="8010"` in PowerShell) and stop it afterwards.
- No automated tests exist; validate with the repo scripts: `node scripts/generate-insights.js --days 90 --top 5`, `npm run sync:jira:test`, `npm run test:sistema-filter`.
- Keep `/api/search` behavior stable — analysts depend on it daily.
- No secrets, passwords, tokens, or personal data in notes, code, or docs.

---

# JARVIS / Dendron — Note Structure Rules

You help the team write Dendron Markdown notes that JARVIS can index and search with high precision.

## Goal

Every closed HD / Jira incident must become a searchable knowledge note: root cause, solution, system, SQL/scripts, and a clear closure section.

## File naming

- Use Dendron hierarchy: `hd.<sistema>.<modulo>.<ticket>.md`
- Examples: `hd.sisnet.reportes.jira-12345.md`, `hd.core.batch.hd-9876.md`
- Keep the Jira/HD key in `title` and preferably in the filename.

## Required frontmatter

```yaml
---
id: jira-12345
title: "JIRA-12345 — Error ORA-00942 en REPORTE_1"
desc: "Breve resumen indexable (error + sintoma)"
updated: 2026-07-30
tags: [hd, sisnet, reporte, oracle]
---
```

Rules:
- `id`: ticket key (Jira/HD), stable and unique.
- `title`: ticket + short symptom (include system/report/error tokens).
- `tags`: lowercase, searchable tokens (system, technology, error class).
- `updated`: ISO date when the note was last corrected.

## Required body sections (exact labels)

Always use these labels so JARVIS regex extraction works:

```markdown
**Sistema:** SISNET
**Módulo:** Reportes
**Reporte:** REPORTE_1
**Tabla:** SCHEMA.TABLE_NAME

**Causa Raíz:**
Explicacion concreta de la causa (no solo el sintoma).

**Solución:**
Pasos exactos para resolver. Incluir comandos y orden de ejecucion.

## ✅ Cierre de HD
Texto listo para pegar en Jira/HD: que se hizo, evidencia, y estado final.
```

## SQL and commands

- Put every SQL statement inside a fenced block with language `sql`:

````markdown
```sql
SELECT * FROM SCHEMA.TABLE_NAME WHERE id = :id;
```
````

- Put shell/PowerShell/Python commands in fenced blocks with the correct language tag (`bash`, `powershell`, `python`).
- Prefer copy-paste ready scripts. Avoid screenshots of SQL.

## Search quality checklist (before saving)

1. Does the title contain the ticket key AND a real symptom token?
2. Are Sistema / Módulo / Causa Raíz / Solución present with the exact labels above?
3. Are table names, report names, and error codes written in plain text (e.g. `ORA-00942`, `REPORTE_1`, `SISNET`)?
4. Is there at least one ` ```sql ` block when SQL was used?
5. Does `## ✅ Cierre de HD` contain a paste-ready closure paragraph?
6. Are tags useful for future teammates who only remember the system or error class?

## Anti-patterns (do NOT)

- Vague titles like "Error en produccion" without system/ticket.
- Solutions buried only in chat screenshots.
- SQL as plain paragraphs without fenced code blocks.
- Renaming labels (`Root Cause`, `Fix`, `System`) — stick to the Spanish labels above for team consistency.
- Putting secrets, passwords, tokens, or personal data in notes.

## When generating a new note from a ticket

1. Extract ticket id, system, module, error text, tables, reports.
2. Write Causa Raíz as the real cause, not the user complaint.
3. Write Solución as ordered steps a teammate can execute at 3am.
4. Add SQL/commands in copyable blocks.
5. Finish with `## ✅ Cierre de HD` ready for the ticket comment.
